            <h3 class="headline">
                <span>Label (label) - Selenium IDE command</span>
            </h3>
        </div> 

        <div class="span12">

            <p> <span class="hired">Label</span> marks the place you want <a href="/rpa/docs/selenium-ide/gotoIf">gotoIf</a> and <a href="/rpa/docs/selenium-ide/gotolabel">gotoLabel</a> to jump to.</p>
                
                
<p><a href="https://ui.vision/docs/selenium-ide#flowcontrol">Flow control</a> is a regular <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> Selenium IDE feature. In the classic Selenium IDE you can add support for flow control by installing the Flow Control plugin.</p>


                <h3>gotoIf Example</h3>
            <p>The example below is very basic. Best if you see the flow logic in action by running the DemoGotoIf macro that installs with the IDE.</p>
            <p>
                <table class="table table-bordered">
                    <thead>
                    <th class="col-md-2">Command</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Target</th>
                    <th class="col-md-5">Pattern/Text</th>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>

                        <tr>
                            <td>open</td>
                            <td>https://ui.vision/</td>
                            <td><br /></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="success">
                            <td>Label</td>
                            <td>MYLABEL</td>
                            <td></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </p>

            <h3>Works in</h3>
            <p>
                <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> for Chrome <a href="/">Selenium IDE</a>,  <em>Ui.Vision RPA</em> for Firefox <a href="/">Selenium IDE</a>,   <a href="/howto/getseleniumide/">Firefox IDE Classic</a>
            </p>

